A `sed`-style comma range on a file that exists is almost certainly a mistyped `:a-b`, so the miss names the spelling that would have worked.

```console
$ lets edit usage.ts:40,60 --old x --new y
? 1
usage.ts:40,60: no such file · did you mean usage.ts:40-60
ERROR_CODE=not_found

```

The control: a path whose prefix names no file keeps the plain not-found message.

```console
$ lets edit nope.ts --old x --new y
? 1
nope.ts: No such file or directory (os error 2)
ERROR_CODE=not_found

```
